  "actual_cuda_observations": [
    "One original A submission owns key and value PagedAppend transactions. Each source contributes two untouched ready pages, three full writers, and one existing append epoch. The second request has a real COW page.",
    "B has a different query_indptr but the same required KV prefix footprint. Its explicit metadata retains the original real ready mirror lease; no fake ready frame is constructed.",
    "B is recorded before A using only the original physical capacities for metadata/capture preparation, without submitting a reader. Its two typed reader descriptors are also prepared before A.",
    "A is genuinely pending behind an original CUDA Queue host gate while B binds both KV resources through the same concrete output bundle and original SubmissionSource.",
    "B reuses the existing capture with recorded=0/reused=1; dependency reports one source, one device wait, zero host waits. Ordinary submit cannot bypass the ordered permission map.",
    "After A actually retires and detaches, B remains gated while the original bulk take returns both transactions. Key publication makes an original ready_delta and commits a WorkingFrame; value publication and its retry make the original ready frame.",
    "Old key/value layouts and prefixes remain bounded. Fresh/COW partial pages acquire real appenders; reserve on an admitted reader remains unavailable. Final BF16 attention results are exactly 0.5 and 1.0 per request; all selected value rows and old snapshot bytes match."
  ],
  "resource_and_architecture_observations": [
    "ResourceSource cold-reserves fixed ready/full/append metadata and charges the original budget. Capture authenticates the exact submitted parent, selected/nominated writer, registered page set, and real resource/allocator lifetimes.",
    "Source metadata visits temporarily pin original results and release the observation mutex before invoking the existing typed metadata visitor. Capture leaves no writer/appender/transaction pointer retained.",
    "Ready, full and append roots are mutually exclusive in the receiver footprint. An append ticket covers its old prefix without a second ordinary read admission; COW-copy-only source pages are not incorrectly treated as receiver pages.",
    "Every exact append prefix is purely checked before the first writer is sealed. The new pure query shares the original validation formula and cannot export a view, allocate a ticket, or change the epoch/seal.",
    "Token, Store and resource entries retain the same original terminal table, proxy, Queue and whole verdict. A private read-only InputSources query rejects splitting one Invocation into multiple pending bundles, avoiding representative-dependent prepare gates.",
    "The original projected-reader pure checks are shared with atomic bundle binding. Required-ready metadata retains its real block/generation/range and is rechecked at preparation/submission; configuration ownership is preserved.",
    "Fresh conversion only follows successful actual write retirement and exact full-ticket/page identity. Existing readonly uses retire normally; old full tickets cannot admit new readers after appendable conversion. New readers use real bounded ready leases.",
    "Paged publication bridges update the original arena frontier and consume full appenders without relaxing public publish/reserve/rollback. Foreign tickets, bad row counts, reacquired ordinary pages, and failed producer publication reject while old snapshots remain unchanged."
  ],
